      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town became the county seat in 1822 and was platted that same year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shelbyville%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A horse‑drawn railroad began operating in Shelbyville in 1834, making it Indiana’s first railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
